= Thomas J. Fellers
{c}
{parent=List of optical microscopists}

An <optical microscopist> and author of material on <optical microscopes>.<Linear Measurements (Micrometry) by Thomas J. Fellers and Michael W. Davidson>[Contributing Authors: Thomas J. Fellers and Michael W. Davidson, National High Magnetic Field Laboratory, Florida State University]{ref}

= Work by Thomas J. Fellers
{parent=Thomas J. Fellers}

= Optical nonreciprocity
{parent=Optics}

<Optical nonreciprocity> means that exchanging source and detector paths need not restore the corresponding transmission when external conditions, including the <magnetic field>, are held fixed. The <Faraday effect> gives a <linear polarization> rotation with the same laboratory sense on both traversals; see <Faraday rotation on a round trip>.
